    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1cac99f6_0b34d2f8",
        "filename": "kubespray-installer/setup.sh",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 77,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000011
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-06-27T14:09:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1. The admin.conf location changed in the newer commit of kubespray\n\n2. Check the path to the KUBECONFIG file before setting it, so specifying an an incorrect name to the `-s` option prints an error and fails\n\n3. The `set ...` undoes the `set ...` at the top of the file, which make scriptwriting more reliable (bailing if unset variables, or if a command exit with non-zero).  Without this, your interactive shell will act the same way which is bad when a minor typo in a command causes it to exit non-zero and your interactive shell closes abruptly. Scott found this out by experience. :)",
      "parentUuid": "2d760528_57db77e5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 64,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 77,
        "endChar": 4
